body.zh:
把複數寫成 $a+bi$ 之後：$a$ 是實部（real part）、$b$ 是虛部（imaginary part）。兩者都是實數，虛部只寫 $i$ 前面那個數，而且要連符號 —— $3-7i$ 的實部是 $3$、虛部是 $-7$（不是 $7$）。
{{math:0}}
分母有 $i$ 時，分子分母同乘分母的共軛（conjugate），把分母變成實數：$(c+di)(c-di)=c^{2}+d^{2}$。
{{math:1}}
兩個高頻題型：
① 求 real part／imaginary part：先化簡成 $a+bi$，再讀出 $a$、$b$ —— 讀完要核對正負號；
② 「is a real number」（是實數）＝虛部 $=0$：把 $i$ 的係數寫成一條方程，就求得 $k$。
{{math:2}}

body.en:
Once a complex number is written as $a+bi$: $a$ is the real part and $b$ is the imaginary part. Both are real numbers, and the imaginary part is only the number in front of $i$, with its sign — for $3-7i$ the real part is $3$ and the imaginary part is $-7$, not $7$.
{{math:0}}
When the denominator contains $i$, multiply the top and the bottom by the conjugate of the denominator: $(c+di)(c-di)=c^{2}+d^{2}$ makes the denominator real.
{{math:1}}
Two frequent question types:
(1) find the real part or the imaginary part: simplify into $a+bi$ first, then read off $a$ and $b$ and check the signs;
(2) “is a real number” means the imaginary part is $0$: set the coefficient of $i$ equal to zero and solve for $k$.
{{math:2}}

Complex-number questions follow four fixed steps: (1) simplify any power of $i$ first by dividing the index by 4; (2) add, subtract, multiply or divide and tidy everything into the form $a+bi$ using $i^{2}=-1$; (3) when the denominator contains $i$, multiply the top and the bottom by its conjugate so that the denominator becomes $c^{2}+d^{2}$; (4) only then answer what is asked — the real part, the imaginary part, or use “is a real number” to mean that the imaginary part is zero.
{{math:0}}
Five ways marks are lost:
(1) remembering $i^{4}$ as $-1$ instead of $1$, which spoils every higher power;
(2) writing the conjugate product as $c^{2}-d^{2}$ instead of $c^{2}+d^{2}$, because minus $i$ squared is plus 1;
(3) answering the imaginary part when the real part was asked, since the options usually contain both;
(4) dropping the sign of the imaginary part ($2-4i$ has imaginary part $-4$, not $4$);
(5) missing the constant terms that carry no $i$, such as minus $i$ to the 18th being plus 1.

