① 開口方向（$x^2$ 的係數 $a$）；
② 有沒有穿過 $x$ 軸（判別式 $\Delta$）。

寫成一般式 $ax^{2}+bx+c$（$a\ne 0$），「對所有實數 $x$ 都成立」有四種情況：
{{math:0}}

「無解」（沒有任何實數 $x$ 滿足）同樣是看圖：整條拋物線要留在 $x$ 軸的一邊 —— 例如 $ax^{2}+bx+c<0$ 無解，即圖像永遠不會跌到 $x$ 軸下方，所以 $a>0$ 且 $\Delta\le0$（不相交的 $\Delta<0$ 與只相切的 $\Delta=0$ 都符合）。四種情況：
{{math:1}}

三個要點：
① $a>0$（開口向上）才可以「大於 0」撐得住；$a<0$（開口向下）才可以「小於 0」撐得住 —— 只看 $\Delta$ 而漏看 $a$，答案一定錯。
② 有等號（$\ge$、$\le$）用 $\Delta\le 0$；嚴格（$>$、$<$）用 $\Delta<0$。$\Delta=0$ 時只有一個 $x$ 值會令式子等於 0，嚴格不等式不接受那一個值（見上一張卡）。
③ 如果 $x^2$ 的係數含未知數（例如 $kx^{2}+\cdots$），要另外檢查 $k=0$：那時它不是二次式。

例（$a\ne 1$）：$3x^{2}+4x+k>0$ 對所有實數 $x$ 都成立{{math:2}}
例（無解）：$kx^{2}+2x+1<0$ 沒有實數解{{math:3}}

body.en:
“For any real number $x$” means the whole parabola must stay on one side of the $x$-axis, so two things always matter at once:
(1) which way it opens (the coefficient $a$ of $x^{2}$);
(2) whether it crosses the $x$-axis (the discriminant $\Delta$).

Write the quadratic as $ax^{2}+bx+c$ with $a\ne 0$. “True for all real $x$” gives four cases:
{{math:0}}

“No solution” (no real $x$ satisfies it) is read from the graph in the same way: the whole parabola must stay on one side of the $x$-axis — for example, $ax^{2}+bx+c<0$ having no solution means the curve never drops below the $x$-axis, so $a>0$ and $\Delta\le0$ (both missing the axis, $\Delta<0$, and only touching it, $\Delta=0$, qualify). The four cases:
{{math:1}}

Three key points:
(1) $a>0$ (opening upwards) is what lets a quadratic stay positive, and $a<0$ (opening downwards) is what lets it stay negative — using $\Delta$ alone and forgetting $a$ always gives a wrong answer.
(2) With equality ($\ge$, $\le$) use $\Delta\le 0$; for a strict inequality ($>$, $<$) use $\Delta<0$. When $\Delta=0$ there is one value of $x$ that makes the expression zero, and a strict inequality rejects it (see the previous card).
(3) If the coefficient of $x^{2}$ contains the unknown (for example $kx^{2}+\cdots$), check $k=0$ separately: then it is not a quadratic at all.

Example ($a\ne 1$): $3x^{2}+4x+k>0$ for all real $x$ {{math:2}}
Example (no solution): $kx^{2}+2x+1<0$ has no real solution {{math:3}}

